// Round 86 -- Phase A step 1 of the networking/SSH/WiFi scope (see
// project memory project_dhruva_networking_ssh_wifi_scope_2026_09_06
// .md): the smallest useful netif abstraction on this port. Loopback/
// synthetic frames only -- deliberately NOT a real GENET or USB/XHCI
// NIC driver, mirroring how even kernel_main.vani's own Pi 1 side
// verifies its netif layer purely via synthetic frames (its real
// LAN9512/CDC-ECM backends have no QEMU device model either, per
// docs/TODO.md's own Tier 3 list) -- confirmed freshly this round
// that QEMU's raspi4b machine has no network device model at all, so
// a real backend has no QEMU verification path regardless of how this
// is designed. The queue itself lives in boot/rpi4/netif_state.S
// (its own header comment has the full ring-buffer design), the same
// "persistent state lives in a small asm accessor file, vani only
// ever holds transient/local state" shape round 84's shell_state.S
// already established on this port.
// 512, not kernel_main.vani's own current 1514-byte real-Ethernet-MTU
// sizing, deliberately -- that Pi 1 side itself started at exactly
// this same 512 ("deliberately smaller than a real Ethernet MTU,
// since nothing this project could test end-to-end under QEMU needed
// a full-size frame", round 66's own comment) and was only raised
// once a real DHCPOFFER actually needed more. Nothing in this round's
// self-test needs more than 16 bytes -- raise this the same way Pi
// 1's netif_frame_slot_size() was raised, once a real later round's
// payload actually needs it, not speculatively now. Also a practical
// vani-language constraint: vani has no array-repeat literal syntax
// (`[0; N]`) and `let` requires a full initializer, so a fixed-size
// local array needs either a fully hand-enumerated literal or a
// helper returning one (netif_zero_frame_rpi4 below) -- 512 elements
// is a far more tractable one-time literal than 1514.
const NETIF_SLOT_SIZE_RPI4: i64 = 512;

extern "C" fn netif_state_reset() -> u32;
extern "C" fn netif_state_count() -> u32;
extern "C" fn netif_state_stage_byte(offset: u32, value: u32) -> u32;
extern "C" fn netif_state_commit_send(frame_len: u32) -> i64;
extern "C" fn netif_state_recv_len() -> i64;
extern "C" fn netif_state_recv_byte(offset: u32) -> u32;
extern "C" fn netif_state_recv_advance() -> u32;

fn netif_get_mtu_rpi4() -> i64 {
  return NETIF_SLOT_SIZE_RPI4 - 14;
}

// See NETIF_SLOT_SIZE_RPI4's own comment above for why this helper
// exists at all (vani has no array-repeat literal, so this is the
// one and only place a 512-byte zero literal is hand-enumerated).
